{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787949911502569001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"loathful-unanarchic-chickadee","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ee6774295e4f4a5b252d2f3bdd5b0276dbdbb8d2b118222324dda9b79519552f","event_uuid":"6596e834-e2fe-4b36-87d2-f44c5cc6f81e","position":{"commit_sha":"2867a31d9ba8a4c0563f230d97959cb81a627a5e","position":"1787940818450761363-6596e834-e2fe-4b36-87d2-f44c5cc6f81e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dc3a005b19c366e84f543d424d828c31a2c6e7a25e48fa8b5605b2aa8121fdfb","event_uuid":"52a93595-b059-459a-8031-8680a4d3323f","position":{"commit_sha":"190be16b28bf461507c45af7dc232a9b4c861284","position":"1787940848118781856-52a93595-b059-459a-8031-8680a4d3323f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"daaaf6b90a94096f9e8d3a66fdc09461867e0dea99873cb9d1f1e3a7414dc718","event_uuid":"ca565cb9-3c1f-44da-9acb-32411322bb7c","position":{"commit_sha":"6d0194b22dca316c71194919b773beffee40afa4","position":"1787941729452740056-ca565cb9-3c1f-44da-9acb-32411322bb7c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Note: the MCP-endpoint 401 that blocked this session is resolved — client-side, not a server defect\n\nRoot-caused 2026-08-28 (read-only, `/rebar-debug` Phase 1). Not a defect in this ticket's code path and\nno code change needed; recording it here so the next session on this ticket is not blocked by it.\n\n**The endpoint is healthy.** Probed from the box at the same moment, same URL:\n\n- `POST /mcp` `initialize` with the real `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT` -> **200**, full MCP result.\n- `POST /mcp` `initialize` with the string the client actually stores -> **401 `invalid_token` /\n  \"Authentication required\"** (byte-identical to the report).\n\n**The stored credential is not a credential.** `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json`\n`.mcpServers.rebar.headers.Authorization` holds `Bearer ` + a 25-char value whose SHA-256 prefix is\n`49a88ca4…`, which equals `sha256(\"${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT}\")[:12]` — i.e. the literal, unexpanded\nenv-var reference from the committed template (`examples/mcp-clients/copilot/mcp-config.json:23`).\n`MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT` is unset in the operator's login shell, so the client had nothing to expand.\n\n`rebar doctor` already names this exactly, for all three clients:\n\n    copilot [error] pat-unresolvable: ... reads the rebar bearer PAT from MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT,\n    but MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT is unset or empty in this environment ...\n\n**Remediation (operator, per `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` \"Make the export DURABLE\"):** export the three\n`MCP_CLIENT_PAT_*` values persistently, then re-launch the client. Nothing to change on the box —\n`/opt/rebar/infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` is intact (298 bytes, valid JSON, 3 `token_env`\nrecords) and the SSM PATs are still at Version 1 (never rotated).\n\nThe disk-full outage caused the earlier 60s timeouts only; it did **not** corrupt the token store.\nOnce the server came back, the same always-invalid placeholder started getting a correct 401 instead\nof a timeout — which is why it looked like \"auth broke with an unchanged token\".","timestamp":1787941729452740056}],"created_at":1787940818450761363,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"52a93595-b059-459a-8031-8680a4d3323f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c066-c496-7012-4a39"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`rebar claim` (via `claim_gate_check` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py`, which calls\n`signing.verify_signature` -> `verify_opcert_record` in `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:517-535`)\nunconditionally rejects a plan-review op-cert whose `principal` differs from the local\nenvironment's `own_principal`, returning `verdict: \"foreign_key\"` and refusing to claim.\n\nReproduced 2026-08-28: `review_plan` run through the rebar MCP server (principal\n`9f1c8e42-...`) signed and returned `\"signature\":{\"signed\":true}` (a genuine PASS). The\nsubsequent `rebar claim <id>` from this checkout's local CLI/venv (a different environment,\nprincipal `b8a354e0-...`) failed with:\n```\nno certified plan-review attestation (signature: foreign_key; op-cert signed by a different\nenvironment (principal '9f1c8e42-...'; this environment is 'b8a354e0-...'))\n```\nRe-running `review-plan` locally (same environment as the later `claim`) succeeded, confirming\nthe attestation itself was valid — only the environment mismatch blocked the claim.\n\n## Why this is a bug, not intended behavior\n`docs/releasing.md` / AGENTS.md / ADR 0104 decision 3 state that op-cert environment-binding is\n**advisory, not enforced**, until an operator explicitly sets `verify.require_environment` +\n`verify.opcert_enforce_since` together (`infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`). This\nproject's `rebar.toml` sets neither. The standalone `rebar verify-opcert` command (\n`src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`) correctly honors this: \"`verify.require_environment`\nunset -> advisory everywhere (exit 0)\". But the CLAIM-gate path (`verify_opcert_record` in\n`_opcert_signing.py`, reached via `claim_gate_check`) has NO such config check — it hard-rejects\nany cross-environment `principal` unconditionally, regardless of\n`require_environment`/`opcert_enforce_since`. So a project that has NOT opted into environment\nenforcement still cannot claim a ticket whose plan-review was legitimately signed by a different\nenvironment (e.g. the MCP server vs. a local CLI worktree) — the \"advisory\" promise is broken in\npractice for this one gate.\n\n## Impact\nAny agent whose plan-review runs through the rebar MCP server (a different signing environment\nthan its local `rebar` CLI/worktree) cannot claim the ticket it just got PASSED review on, without\neither re-running the review locally (wasteful, doubles LLM cost) or a human using `--force`\n(policy-disallowed for agents). This directly blocked cutting the rebar 0.13.0 release ticket.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Have two environments configured with different `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` (e.g. the MCP server\n   container vs. a local checkout), neither `verify.require_environment` nor\n   `verify.opcert_enforce_since` set in `rebar.toml`.\n2. Run `review-plan <ticket>` via environment A (e.g. rebar-mcp) -> PASS, signed.\n3. Run `rebar claim <ticket>` from environment B (local CLI).\n4. Observe `foreign_key` denial, even though environment enforcement is not configured.\n\n## Suggested fix\n`claim_gate_check` / `verify_opcert_record`'s claim-path check should consult\n`verify.require_environment` + `verify.opcert_enforce_since` (mirroring `verify_opcert.py`'s\nlogic) before treating a cross-environment `principal` as disqualifying. When enforcement is not\nconfigured, a structurally-valid signed attestation from ANY environment should satisfy the claim\ngate (still validating the DSSE/sshsig signature itself when the verifying environment has the\nmatching public key; when it does not, the enforcement-off path should not fail the claim solely\nfor that reason).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: With `verify.require_environment`/`opcert_enforce_since` unset, `rebar claim` accepts a certified plan-review attestation signed by a different registered environment (no `foreign_key` denial).\n- [ ] AC2: With `verify.require_environment` + `opcert_enforce_since` both set (enforcement flipped on), `rebar claim` still rejects an attestation from an environment other than the required one, or one predating the enforcement pin.\n- [ ] AC3: A regression test in `tests/unit/` covers both the advisory (AC1) and enforced (AC2) configurations for the claim-gate path specifically (not just `verify-opcert`).\n- [ ] AC4: `docs/plan-review-gate.md` documents this cross-environment acceptance behavior and its interaction with the enforcement flip.\n\n## Testing\n- New/updated tests exercising `claim_gate_check` / `verify_opcert_record` under both configs.\n- `make test` passes.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c21f-6f29-5d2d-4a5a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Claim gate hard-rejects cross-environment plan-review op-certs even when environment enforcement is not configured","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6596e834-e2fe-4b36-87d2-f44c5cc6f81e","52a93595-b059-459a-8031-8680a4d3323f","ca565cb9-3c1f-44da-9acb-32411322bb7c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787949911502569001,"uuid":"0eb12e39-c12f-4eac-97a8-d43d2bd9aeaf"}